         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/98a5dcc5-7d4c-4265-ad51-bac48b11b123,1792008869540/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%28149%2C0%2C2414%2C1357%29%3B' alt='Ontario Minister of Colleges and Universities Nolan Quinn speaks during Question Period in the Ontario Legislature in Toronto on Tuesday March 24, 2026. THE CANADIAN PRESS/Frank Gunn' width='620' height='349' title='Ontario Minister of Colleges and Universities Nolan Quinn speaks during Question Period in the Ontario Legislature in Toronto on Tuesday March 24, 2026. THE CANADIAN PRESS/Frank Gunn'/><p>Ontario's colleges and universities minister has barred three career colleges from being able to offer publicly funded student financial assistance until at least 2030, after previously blocking them from the program just for this year.</p>]]></description>
